-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Atom Ant
  Publisher   Hi-Tec, 1990
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Atom Ant (1990)(Hi-Tec)(48K-128K).tap
  MD5         404e992b4edceb10ef8fae9dfaac364b

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. Game logic is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu,
  are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Ynicky's Spec256 colours as the set paints them: a red-brown
              city with orange bricks, pale windows, green Atom Ant, painted
              enemies and items, and the coloured panel. Nothing repainted.
              Source: Enhanced colours: Ynicky (Spec256).

  Pace        original (+0.10% measured in JNext 1.1.104, against the tape's
              start state as a .z80 on a 128K machine, at the player's update,
              input applied after the game's read, game state in lockstep)

  Changes     1.0: the 128K form of the tape, its AY music kept; the original
              look; the tape's own loading screen; three cheats from the
              archive, tested; Enhanced colours from the Spec256 set on a
              double-buffered Layer 2, off by default

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 1 keyboard (Q up, A down, O left, P
              right, SPACE fire), 2 Kempston, 3 Interface 2. In play F pauses,
              a control key resumes, G quits to the menu. Default: the
              original look, white on black, with no clash fix to claim, and
              the 128K tape's AY music. Enhanced, on the menu, off by default:
              the Spec256 colours on Layer 2 over the unchanged game, all
              seven levels. Needs the .tap. Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues:
              pace in JNext: default +0.00%; Enhanced -0.46% to +0.10% over
              whole runs, quiet thirds -1.13% to -0.29%, busy thirds +0.06% to
              +0.67%, 12 runs on 4 levels; slowest 20-update stretch +1.02%.
              In Enhanced the panel's digits and the menus keep the original
              colours. Missing: natural play to the end (later levels and
              level ends by a test copy only); Interface 2 not tried; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity
   3  Infinite time

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

